Accidental Insurance does Not include: (a) Terminal Illness;
(b) Pre-Existing Disease; (c) Traffic Mis-Haps;
(d) Industrial Mis-Haps.

Accidental Insurance does Not include: (a) Mental Disorders;
(b) Injuries in Daily Activities;
(c) Injuries caused, while at Duty; (d) Pre-Existing Physical Disorders.

A Personal Accident Policy covers:
(a) Death, arising out of an Accident; (b) Permanent Total Disability;
(c) Illness;
(d) Pregnancy-Complications.

Choose the Right Statement: Endorsement, normally required under a Policy, relates to:
a) Transfer of Property to Another Location;
b) Cancellation of Insurance.
